# Documentation Hub Spec

## Scope

Multi-documentation publishing, guide editing, navigation, discovery, and the
forum-owned documentation presentation adapter.

## Load when

Changing `/doc`, `/forum/docs`, documentation records/routes/editor/search,
forum documentation projection, documentation SEO/cache/realtime, or migration
036.

## Owns

- Backend: `backend/internal/documentation/*`, `backend/models/documentation.go`
- API mount: `/api/docs`; forum projection: `GET /api/forum/documentation`
- Tables: `documentations`, `documentation_sections`, `documentation_articles`
- Frontend: `frontend/src/pages/documentation/*`,
  `frontend/src/components/documentation/*`, `frontend/src/atoms/documentation.ts`
- Shared rich text: `frontend/src/components/ui/RichTextEditor.tsx`,
  `frontend/src/components/ui/RichTextRenderer.tsx`
- Public routes: `/doc`, `/doc/:documentationSlug`,
  `/doc/:documentationSlug/:articleSlug`, `/forum/docs`,
  `/forum/docs/:categoryId`, `/forum/docs/:categoryId/:threadId`
- Authenticated management routes: `/doc/new`,
  `/doc/manage/:documentationSlug/settings`,
  `/doc/manage/:documentationSlug/guides/new`, and
  `/doc/manage/:documentationSlug/guides/:articleSlug`

## Domain Contracts

- One tenant may own any number of documentation sets. Each active set and each
  active article within a set has a case-insensitive unique slug.
- A set has an owner, title, description, visibility (`public`, `unlisted`, or
  `private`), ordered sections/articles, and an optimistic revision.
- Articles store sanitized-renderer-compatible TipTap HTML, summary, optional
  section, display order, and an optimistic revision. Section deletion moves
  its active articles to the ungrouped overview; it does not delete them.
- Public sets are cataloged and indexed. Unlisted sets resolve by link but are
  absent from catalog/search/sitemap. Private reads require owner or
  `docs.manage`. `docs.create` creates sets; owner or `docs.manage` mutates.
- All list/search payloads are bounded. Search returns article identity/title,
  summary/snippet, and section label without sending every article body.
- Deletes are retained lifecycle transitions exposed through Trash providers;
  active reads, slug uniqueness, navigation, search, and SEO exclude tombstones.
- Update revision mismatch returns `409`; the client preserves its draft and
  requires an authoritative refetch before another save.

## API Shape

| Method/path | Contract |
| --- | --- |
| `GET/POST /api/docs` | public set catalog / create set |
| `GET /api/docs/mine` | owned sets, or every active set for `docs.manage` |
| `GET/PUT/DELETE /api/docs/{slug}` | manifest / metadata update / retained delete |
| `GET /api/docs/{slug}/articles/{articleSlug}` | article with previous/next navigation |
| `GET /api/docs/{slug}/search?q=` | bounded visible article search |
| `POST /api/docs/id/{id}/sections` | create ordered section |
| `PUT/DELETE /api/docs/sections/{id}` | rename / retained section delete |
| `POST /api/docs/id/{id}/articles` | create guide |
| `PUT/DELETE /api/docs/articles/{id}` | revisioned update / retained delete |
| `PUT /api/docs/id/{id}/navigation` | owner-checked section/article ordering |
| `GET /api/forum/documentation?q=` | categories plus bounded thread summaries; no thread bodies |

## Frontend Contracts

- `integrate/` is a UX reference only. The implementation uses GWP routing,
  tokens, permissions, API utilities, Prompt, WebSocket, and existing content;
  it does not import the reference corpus, router, fonts, or app shell.
- `DocumentationShell` owns responsive sidebar/search/navigation, mobile scrim,
  top bar, on-page heading outline, and previous/next links. Drawer controls are
  focusable, labeled, Escape-dismissible, and token styled.
- Documentation article heroes use the compact global `h3` scale in both the
  canonical and forum-backed readers so long guide titles do not dominate the
  reading surface.
- `/doc` reuses the shared `DirectoryLayout`, `FilterBar`, persisted grid/list
  view control, and `TableView`; documentation does not maintain a parallel
  catalog shell. The new-collection action belongs inside the shared filter bar.
- Sidebar search is a single width-constrained searchbox with an icon overlay
  and ellipsized placeholder/content; accessibility copy must not become visible
  layout content. Creation, collection settings/section management, and guide
  editing are dedicated authenticated routes rather than inline reader forms.
  Forms use bounded panels, explicit visible field labels, useful examples, and
  one-column phone layouts; reading routes remain read-only surfaces.
- The guide create/edit route reuses the same routed-form surface as New Thread
  and New Product: one bordered `.modal` with a `.compact-form-card` body, an X
  cancel action and form-associated check submit action in the header, and no
  duplicate primary save control below the editor.
- The forum editor and documentation editor are the same `RichTextEditor`
  boundary. Read-only HTML always passes through `RichTextRenderer`.
- A custom-page `resource_embed` configured for documentation stores only a
  documentation slug. It mounts the normal visibility-aware documentation route
  content with that explicit slug, loads the first visible guide, and retains the
  route's shell, search, navigation, actions, `RichTextRenderer`, subscriptions,
  and canonical `/doc` links. The global app layout is not duplicated inside the
  section. Height is natural unless the page author sets the shared section
  `max_height`, in which case the expanded section owns the scroll boundary. The
  embed never copies documentation records into `pages.content`.
- In-app link navigation while editing uses GWP's Prompt through the
  declarative-`BrowserRouter` compatible dirty-navigation guard; data-router-only
  `useBlocker` and native unload/confirm/prompt/alert dialogs are forbidden.
  Realtime events do not overwrite an active draft.
- `/forum/docs` is only a view adapter. It reads forum categories/thread
  summaries, fetches the selected authoritative thread, reuses forum comments,
  and sends edits to the existing `/edit-thread/:threadId` route. It never
  copies forum rows to documentation tables or owns a second forum editor.
- Category/thread deep links use numeric authoritative IDs so rename/move does
  not orphan a guide; canonical navigation follows the current category.

## Realtime, Cache, and SEO

- `documentation:update` is a content-free invalidation. Public catalog changes
  may broadcast only `catalog_invalidated`; set/article identity goes only to
  authorized `documentation:{id}` or `documentation_article:{id}` subscribers.
- Subscription callbacks are service-backed and fail closed for private data.
  Reconnect and relevant trash restore events trigger authoritative REST refetch.
- Documentation mutations invalidate exact SSR paths and the documentation SEO
  namespace. Forum thread mutations invalidate both normal and forum-doc paths.
- SSR resolves public/unlisted set and guide metadata. The sitemap includes
  `/doc`, `/forum/docs`, and dynamic active public set/guide paths only.
- Documentation management routes resolve the SPA shell with `noindex` before
  public documentation slug lookup; direct navigation must not become a cached
  documentation-not-found response.

## Invariants

- Documentation and forum storage never converge or shadow one another.
- Ownership/permissions are enforced in services, not trusted from route guards.
- WebSocket payloads never contain guide bodies, private titles, slugs, or
  summaries for clients that have not passed resource authorization.
- Rich text extension and sanitization registries remain shared; do not create a
  documentation-only serialization dialect.

## Verify

- `env GOCACHE=/tmp/skaia-go-cache GOTMPDIR=/tmp JWT_SECRET=test-secret go test ./...` from `backend/`
- `npm run lint && npm test -- --run && npm run check:native-dialogs && npm run build` from `frontend/`
- `rg "documentations|documentation_sections|documentation_articles" backend/internal/migrations`
- `rg "documentation:update|/forum/docs|/doc/" backend frontend/src`

